        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The right humidifier size is the one whose daily output matches the moisture your space loses. Start with the chart, adjust for ceiling height, open doorways, air leakage, outdoor cold and heating type, and size up when you land between two rows.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Then measure. A hygrometer across the room will tell you within two days whether you guessed right, and it is the only way to catch the more expensive mistake of running too much humidity into a cold house.
          </p>
